   "interpretation": "Reference state. The homogeneous zigzag sheet stores 6.7 J/m2 before a single instability at 27% strain breaks every load-bearing bond row at once (36 bonds in one increment); the dip at 18% is the transverse-branch switch of the model. Failure initiates nowhere in particular: all bonds along the load are equivalent, so there is no load path to redistribute to, and the fracture is maximally abrupt. Every porous design is weaker than this state, but many retain load after their peak, which the pristine sheet cannot."
