   "interpretation": "Flaw-sensitivity reference. Bonds first break at the two crack tips at 8.1% strain, the crack then runs straight across the sheet perpendicular to the load in one avalanche at 8.6% (18.5 N/m). Damage is confined to the crack plane (L = 0.52). Compared with the 10 A crack (24.1 N/m) the strength loss follows a Griffith-like trend, but the 30-50 A cracks do not weaken further: in this lattice the tip-bond configuration, not the crack length, sets the instability once the flaw exceeds ~20 A."
